X2 <- fitMeasures(fit)[["chisq"]]
X2.null <- fitMeasures(fit)[["baseline.chisq"]]
df <- fitMeasures(fit)[["df"]]
df.null <- fitMeasures(fit)[["baseline.df"]]

t1 <- max( c(X2 - df, 0) )
t2 <- max( c(X2 - df, X2.null - df.null, 0) )
cfi  <- 1 - t1/t2

cfi

(untested code).

Or you could just write:
X2 <- fitMeasures(fit)[["cfi"]]

I'm not clear what your goal is. If your goal is to understand how lavaan works, you could look at the code, or look at articles that have the equations. If your goal is to get CFI, you can use the fitMeasures() function. (Or is your goal something else?)

