Hi Mauricio,

based on Yves slides <https://eeecon.uibk.ac.at/~psychoco-2012/2020/slides/Rosseel.pdf> I added bounds=T and the estimation ends normally after 400 iterations. Unfortunately, this way non of the regressions get significant as I would expect from previous correlation analysis or when using the growth curve factors in posterior analysis (I know its bad practice).

Allowing 20000 iterations to reach a solution as described here <https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/multilevel.html> results in the error:
lavdata@nlevels > 1L is not TRUE

